RUN: %COMPILE_IR %S/guarded_return.cfc | %CHECK_IR %s

The diagram, with execution orders in parentheses:

guard --> RETURN (0)
42 -----> result (1)

Each ordered element must get a debug location in the diagram's own file,
at line = order + 1, so a debugger can break on it.

Guard load, branch and return are one element (order 0); the store is the sink (order 1).
The instructions are matched inside the function, so no other function's instructions can bind.
CHECK-LABEL: define void @guarded_return(ptr %0) !dbg ![[#SCOPE_FUNCTION:]]
CHECK:       %load_guard = load i8, ptr %guard, {{.*}}!dbg ![[#LOCATION_RETURN:]]
CHECK:       br i1 %{{[0-9]+}}, label %then_block, label %else_block, !dbg ![[#KEY_GUARD:]]
CHECK:       then_block:
CHECK-NEXT:  ret void, !dbg ![[#KEY_RETURN:]]
CHECK:       else_block:
CHECK-NEXT:  store i32 42, ptr %result, {{.*}}!dbg ![[#KEY_RESULT:]]

Debug file per area: declaration text vs. diagram `guarded_return`.
CHECK-DAG: ![[#FILE_DECLARATION:]] = !DIFile(filename: "guarded_return.cfc", directory:
CHECK-DAG: ![[#FILE_DIAGRAM:]] = !DIFile(filename: "guarded_return.cfc.guarded_return", directory:

The function lives in the declaration; a lexical block inside it is bound to the diagram file.
The function places its stops by Key Instructions.
CHECK-DAG: ![[#SCOPE_FUNCTION]] = distinct !DISubprogram(name: "guarded_return", {{.*}}, file: ![[#FILE_DECLARATION]], line: 1, {{.*}}keyInstructions: true)
CHECK-DAG: ![[#SCOPE_DIAGRAM:]] = distinct !DILexicalBlock(scope: ![[#SCOPE_FUNCTION]], file: ![[#FILE_DIAGRAM]])

Diagram statements are scoped to that block, line = execution order + 1 (0 is reserved).
CHECK-DAG: ![[#LOCATION_RETURN]] = !DILocation(line: 1, scope: ![[#SCOPE_DIAGRAM]])

The last side effect of an element in each block is a key instruction, the only place a debugger
stops: the return element has two, its guard branch and the return behind it.
CHECK-DAG: ![[#KEY_GUARD]] = !DILocation(line: 1, scope: ![[#SCOPE_DIAGRAM]], atomGroup: [[#]], atomRank: 1)
CHECK-DAG: ![[#KEY_RETURN]] = !DILocation(line: 1, scope: ![[#SCOPE_DIAGRAM]], atomGroup: [[#]], atomRank: 1)
CHECK-DAG: ![[#KEY_RESULT]] = !DILocation(line: 2, scope: ![[#SCOPE_DIAGRAM]], atomGroup: [[#]], atomRank: 1)
